What integer is printed by the following C program?
```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int m[2][4] = {{1, 3, 5, 7}, {2, 4, 6, 8}};
    int *p = &m[0][0];
    printf("%d", *(p + 5) + *(p + 2));
    return 0;
}
```

What integer is printed by the following C program?
```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int a[6] = {11, 22, 33, 44, 55, 66};
    int *p = a + 1;
    int *q = a + 5;
    printf("%d", (int)(q - p) + (*q - *p));
    return 0;
}
```

Consider the following pseudocode with nested procedures:
```text
int x = 10;
void f() { print(x); }
void g() { int x = 20; f(); }
void main() { g(); }
```
What is printed under (i) Static (lexical) scoping and (ii) Dynamic scoping?
